  "version": "1.4.0",
  "schema": "ir_catalog/canonical",
  "_doc": "Brand-neutral IR role catalog. Robots map ONTO this; never auto-extended from URDF/USDA. Source: DEMO/src/system/training/ir_role_catalog.py. v1.1.0: biped/humanoid expanded with multi-DOF joint roles (hip/ankle/shoulder/wrist axis-split + waist/neck/fingers) to cover Unitree G1 (29 DOF) / H1 (19 DOF) / G1 with_hands fingers. v1.2.0: family-agnostic `sensor` role family (sensor / sensor_imu / sensor_lidar / sensor_camera / sensor_radar / sensor_gps / sensor_sonar / sensor_depth) for non-actuated mount links (replaces ad-hoc Out-of-Scope for IMU/camera mounts). v1.3.0: added family-agnostic `misc` role (category `misc`) for physical-but-non-actuated cosmetic links (Go2's base_black / base_white / *_protector / *_calflower); both `misc` and `sensor_*` are dedupe-exempt because they legitimately cover many entries per robot. Three-tier semantics: limb role (actuated) > sensor_* (perception) > misc (physical decoration) > __out_of_scope__ (virtual helpers like USD AssemblerFixedJoint). v1.4.0: removed the bogus quadruped `ankle_FL/FR/RL/RR` roles added in v1.2.0. They were introduced under the false premise that BD Spot has a 4th-DOF ankle per leg; in fact Spot has 3 actuated DOFs per leg (hip_AA / hip_FE / knee) and the `*_ank` prim in Spot's USD is a FixedJoint attaching the foot rigid body to the lower leg — zero DOF, not an articulation joint. discover_usd_bodies.py now filters to RevoluteJoint/PrismaticJoint only, so phantom ankle joints no longer reach the registry.",
